<title>CANADA: BCE unit launches India cell phone network.</title>
<headline>BCE unit launches India cell phone network.</headline>
<dateline>MONTREAL 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>BCE Inc unit Bell Canada International (BCI) said on Thursday that it launched with its partner Tata Group a cellular telephone network in the Indian state of Andhra Pradesh.</p>
<p>Operating under the name Tata Communications, the new company is licenced to serve the nearly 70 million residents, 850 large-scale enterprises and 100,000 small businesses in India's fifth-largest state, BCI said.</p>
<p>As stipulated under Indian foreign ownership rules, 51 percent of the equity in the cellular and basic telephone companies is held by the Tata Group, BCI said.</p>
</text>
